  "development_findings": [
    "Clang rejected implicit narrowing to 16-bit polygon indices in the new synthetic fixture. Fixed with explicit bounded casts.",
    "The old worldpaths.subway test expected 232 objects; the unchanged baseline collision implementation also produced 233. Exact expectation updated to 233; both implementations retain 297 moves, 2 blocks, identical final state, 11 attachments and clean unload over two cycles."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "CPU diagnostic timings exclude GPU, ImGui and real audio-device scheduling. Debug wrapper/app scene units use -O2 with actual -O0 game/engine libraries.",
    "Fixed-step diagnostic NEW_LEVEL during SubwayA intro, not a human playthrough.",
    "No change to CPU skinning, frustum culling, AI cadence or gameplay tuning.",
    "Remaining user reports and required M2 services stay open. Native Metal not retested."
